---
import ListItem from "../components/ListItem.astro";
import Panel from "../components/Panel.astro";
---

<Panel>
    <h1>Development Skills</h1>
    <p>API design (4+ years experience)</p>
    <ListItem title="API design" subtitle="(4+ years experience)"
        >After 3 years of maintaining and version-bumping existing APIs, an
        opportunity arose in which I was able to co-design a set of brand new
        APIs. Hence, I used my experience with the shortcomings of our existing
        APIs to design something better, including improving REST compliance
        (and thus ease of both database operations and pubsub emissions),
        standardizing our units (eliminating the need for per-stakeholder
        exceptions), and switching off of string-encoded integers (eliminating
        problematic edge cases).
    </ListItem>
    <ListItem title="API implementation" subtitle="(4+ years experience)">
        I've not only implemented and consumed APIs using a number of different
        frameworks (Haskell/Servant, Kotlin/Ktor, TypeScript/Express), but I've
        also dealt with WebSockets, JWTs, OpenAPI docs generation, and writing
        custom middleware.
    </ListItem>
    <ListItem title="Cybersecurity Research">
        <ul>
            <li>
                While working as a research assistant, I used the Binary
                Analysis Platform's symbolic microexecutor to automatically
                verify null reference vulnerabilities in C. Symbolic execution
                was chosen because it's a middle ground between fuzzing (which
                lacks in completeness) and static analysis (which lacks in
                soundness).
            </li>
            <li>
                From my undergraduate and graduate cybersecurity research I've
                also gained experience in binary exploitation (using
                cutter/Ghidra for decompilation and GDB for runtime analysis)
                and network exploitation (e.g. patching XSS and SQL injection
                vulnerabilities).
            </li>
        </ul>
    </ListItem>
</Panel>
